{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1275597-successor-to-the-hollow-ones","id":1275597,"title":"Successor to the Hollow Ones","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-12-20T12:29:01-08:00","id":1275597,"title":"Successor to the Hollow Ones","content":"Over the 20th century, there have been three new Traditions in the form of the SoE (embodies a spirit of progress and science as a solution to problems), VAs (embodies the idea that information and its access is a right that can bring freedom), and Hollow Ones (postmodernism or deconstructionist, all previous metanarratives have failed). Those are very rough considerations which one could pick apart. I feel like the Hollow Ones are reflection of Gen Xs disillusionment. What would be the &quot;next&quot; Tradition? What narrative would embody the Gen Y and Gen Z mages and what would that Tradition look like?<br /> <br /> Just spit-balling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T12:51:10-08:00","id":1275606,"title":"","content":"The Hollow Ones are much older than the 20th century - they started IIRC with the Romanticist movement.The Etherites too are more of a 19th century group too, and the VAs existed long before the rise of hacker culture. I wouldn't think a whole faction would be based on a generational shift.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1410,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","user":"Czernobog","date":". 08-05-2019, 05:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T14:10:12-08:00","id":1275626,"title":"","content":"Let me clarify, each of those traditions has older roots certainly but they captured a zeitgeist that made them appropriate for the times. In the same way neo paganism has been a boon to the Verbena and the growth of awareness of indigenous cultures have helped some groups, I wonder if there's an extant group maybe that aligns with the sentiments of the 21st century in such a way they would suddenly have prominence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T14:34:19-08:00","id":1275628,"title":"","content":"In my games I usually trace the Hollowers back through a wide range of subcultures, including but not limited to biohackers, Homocore, pre-hair band metal, London's Blitz Kids, the German Exis, rockabilly greasers, beatniks, the Lost Generation, Dadaism, the Decadent Movement, the 19th century Bohemians, the 18th and 19th century Romantics, the Sturm und Drang movement, and so on, with the idea that something like this - Mages who dig up mystic secrets and tricks from the forgotten corners of the World of Darkness and seem to be keenly aware of some of it's more morbid truths - has been going on in some shape or fashion since at least the days of Roman street magicians. It's only been in the early 20th century that the Traditions finally put a name to it. As long as there are people who feel alienated from society at large and have a fascination for the dark and weird, there will be Hollow Ones. <br /> <br /> As for what's next, I'm honestly hard pressed to think of anything that's not already covered by the existing groups. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T14:45:12-08:00","id":1275633,"title":"","content":"I don't think the Hollowers would get &quot;replaced&quot;. They might change a bit, adapt, but not disappear. Because it's not the zeitgeist trappings that matter, not that &quot;they are goth&quot;, but the underlying principles. They might just take a new form to express that. Also, it's not like that disillusionment went out of fashion, IMO. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, I can't really come up with any contemporary zeitgeist phenomenon that wasn't covered in one of the existing groups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T16:22:06-08:00","id":1275657,"title":"","content":"Mirai Nohmen, I mean I don't think they replace any of the above but I've always thought the extremely complicated construction of functional paradigms by various Light Novels, video games, anime should have its own group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T16:53:41-08:00","id":1275662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1275597-successor-to-the-hollow-ones?p=1275657#post1275657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mirai Nohmen, I mean I don't think they replace any of the above but I've always thought the extremely complicated construction of functional paradigms by various Light Novels, video games, anime should have its own group.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not familiar with the medium and googling didn't much explain. Can you outline something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T21:49:54-08:00","id":1275720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PhillyCuriosity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1275597-successor-to-the-hollow-ones?p=1275662#post1275662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not familiar with the medium and googling didn't much explain. Can you outline something?</div> </div> </div> </div>For example if you look at say the FATE series you have a fully realized methodology for magic, cosmology etc. And its not particularly unique among Anime/light Novels/video games. So I've always imagined an Otakuish Craft would be a thing<br /> <br /> The closest we've seen to mention of it was Mirai Nohmen","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-21T05:08:08-08:00","id":1275764,"title":"","content":"So...cosplayers?.<br /> <br /> I think that they're better represented by an updated Holow faction, since adapting paradigms from fiction it's a very &quot;chaos magic&quot; thing to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-22T08:59:41-08:00","id":1276058,"title":"","content":"Most magical groups, as social gatherings, are permeable and changeable. They may no longer be so Goth - way too 1990s at this point - but a new version of Hollow Ones could easily be in protest movements, in counter-culture arts movements and the like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-22T10:29:07-08:00","id":1276079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1275597-successor-to-the-hollow-ones?p=1276058#post1276058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most magical groups, as social gatherings, are permeable and changeable. They may no longer be so Goth - way too 1990s at this point - but a new version of Hollow Ones could easily be in protest movements, in counter-culture arts movements and the like.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would want the Holowers anything but going the V5 Brujah route. They are not political activists.<br /> <br /> Also, goth, while changing itself, is still a thing. But regardless, the Hollowers were never &quot;just goths&quot;. Ok, maybe at the beginning, but certanily not in the rEvised tradbook.<br /> <br /> They would totally go for underground arts, music and different subcultures, including maybe otakus and CPers, I think. everything which is about self-expression, stories, romanticism, larger than life things and such. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-22T12:08:34-08:00","id":1276104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1275597-successor-to-the-hollow-ones?p=1276079#post1276079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would want the Holowers anything but going the V5 Brujah route.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh come on. the differences between the Hollow Ones and the Bruja are night and day.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1275597-successor-to-the-hollow-ones?p=1276079#post1276079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are not political activists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not?<br /> <br /> Aside from fact that essentially everything is political, there should be plenty of narrative drama possible in a game involving political cause - trying to push people one way, trying to protect them from the opposition, etc. Things normal people do, but here influenced by magic. And a big part of why the Traditions lost the Ascension War is they were not involved in society and politics. That meant they abandoned those fields to others. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-22T12:34:31-08:00","id":1276107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1275597-successor-to-the-hollow-ones?p=1276104#post1276104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh come on. the differences between the Hollow Ones and the Bruja are night and day.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, exactly because of that, I don't want them to be like the V5 Brujah.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why not?<br /> <br /> Aside from fact that essentially everything is political, </div> </div> </div>Disagree, but hey, you do you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> there should be plenty of narrative drama possible in a game involving political cause - trying to push people one way, trying to protect them from the opposition, etc. Things normal people do, but here influenced by magic. And a big part of why the Traditions lost the Ascension War is they were not involved in society and politics. That meant they abandoned those fields to others. </div> </div> </div>Look, half of the Awakened groups, or more have a political angle and agenda. The Hollowers are not like that. They aren't even an organized group. They are actively against leaders and following big causes. Sure, individual members, even full covens, or chantries could dedicate themselves to political activism, but the group in general, I want them to stay centered around, for a lack of better word, &quot;artsy&quot; things, subcultures, romanticism, modern mysticism, being an outsider, etc. They are a group about finding your own way and truths and expessing yourself and helping others to do that. That could be political activism for some, but it's not a central theme.<br /> <br /> I want them to remain that way.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-22T12:59:12-08:00","id":1276110,"title":"","content":"While the traditions have a political agenda, none seem to do a great job of interfacing directly with mundane political power. Verbena and Dreamspeakers are mentioned as being part of the green movement but maybe another group would work more directly with with people in power rather than strictly trying to motivate sleepers. A craft of essentially &quot;good guy&quot; NWO/Syndicate types seems like it could a vein to bear ore. It'd certainly work at the cabal level, I wonder if it would scale up.<br /> <br /> This could also give a fascinating peek into what countermeasures may exist to prevent a Kindred from Dominating the president or using Presence on a large city council or what have you. This would break down at some point and a power grab in some developing nation of someone using Mind 3/Correspondence 3 would be interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-22T13:40:48-08:00","id":1276115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1275597-successor-to-the-hollow-ones?p=1275764#post1275764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So...cosplayers?.<br /> <br /> I think that they're better represented by an updated Holow faction, since adapting paradigms from fiction it's a very &quot;chaos magic&quot; thing to do.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not quite cosplayers. Though there might be cosplayers among them but rather crazy level otaku who argue about the physics of Final fantasy games. I don't see the mechanically as different from the Hollow Ones but I don't see a social interaction. I don't think the Hollow ONes should cover all orphan spawned groups? Honestly I'd find them a more Mystical Etherites than how Hollow Ones are currently presented.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-22T13:49:18-08:00","id":1276116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1275597-successor-to-the-hollow-ones?p=1275720#post1275720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For example if you look at say the FATE series you have a fully realized methodology for magic, cosmology etc. And its not particularly unique among Anime/light Novels/video games. So I've always imagined an Otakuish Craft would be a thing<br /> <br /> The closest we've seen to mention of it was Mirai Nohmen</div> </div> </div> </div>An Otaku craft? But the things nerds like are style which cribs from different genres with each show/game/comic. So that is as broad as saying like a fiction craft, or Jedi Knight crafts?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I\u2019m thinking next big thing could be a Knights of Avalon Craft, Scientists separated from the Technocracy and thus more open to at least the possibility of mysticism, with the goal of saving the world from those pulling the puppet strings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-23T02:09:24-08:00","id":1276200,"title":"","content":"Kind of like the Society of Ether\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-23T13:52:05-08:00","id":1276310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1275597-successor-to-the-hollow-ones?p=1276200#post1276200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kind of like the Society of Ether\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>The Technocratic Craft could practice both Technocratic Enlightened Science and Mystical Magick, instead of combining the two into Technomagick. I think there is a distinct difference between these two approaches. ( Also - I think that Technomagick can be reached and practiced in other ways. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 12-23-2018, 05:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-23T14:25:55-08:00","id":1276321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1275597-successor-to-the-hollow-ones?p=1276310#post1276310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Technocratic Craft could practice both Technocratic Enlightened Science and Mystical Magick, instead of combining them into Technomagick. I think there is a distinct difference between these two approaches.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't think they could I think a CRAFT could but I don't think something that comes from a Technocratic base position wouldn't have a full mixing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-23T20:14:55-08:00","id":1276361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1275597-successor-to-the-hollow-ones?p=1276310#post1276310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Technocratic Craft could practice both Technocratic Enlightened Science and Mystical Magick, instead of combining the two into Technomagick. I think there is a distinct difference between these two approaches. ( Also - I think that Technomagick can be reached and practiced in other ways. )</div> </div> </div> </div>The Society of Ether as a whole doesn't practice the combining of Enlightened Science and Mystical Magick into a blended Technomagick; they're focused primarily on applying a Scientific mindset to a wider array of possibilities than the Technocratic Union permits (up to and including subjects that would normally be considered fundamentally mystical, like Witchcraft or High Ritual Magick; but more often focusing on fringe science or so-called \u201cpseudo-science\u201d, and sometimes going to the opposite extreme of favoring Practices that one would be hard-pressed to distinguish from what the Technocracy practices). <br /> <br /> If anything, a Craft leaning more towards the aforementioned Technomagick \u2014 something that takes a more mystical approach to what would otherwise be called Enlightened Science \u2014 might be a possibility. I don't see Navalon filling that role, though: it's too much of an inversion of the mindset that the Technocracy has to fit a Craft that is essentially a \u201ckinder and gentler Technocracy\u201d. Rather, I'd see such a Craft emerging from the Traditions, specifically from the subgroups of the various Traditions that already practice such Technomagick (I'm looking at you, House Verditius). <br /> <br /> Or just look at the Virtual Adepts: they tend to have a very mystical view about Information, and their notion of the Hypersphere (i.e., the Correspondence Point being at the center of reality, and the Digital Web filling the \u201cspace\u201d between it and the rest of reality) has a very Techgnostic bent to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 12-23-2018, 11:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-23T22:27:44-08:00","id":1276382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1275597-successor-to-the-hollow-ones?p=1276361#post1276361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Society of Ether as a whole doesn't practice the combining of Enlightened Science and Mystical Magick into a blended Technomagick; they're focused primarily on applying a Scientific mindset to a wider array of possibilities than the Technocratic Union permits (up to and including subjects that would normally be considered fundamentally mystical, like Witchcraft or High Ritual Magick; but more often focusing on fringe science or so-called \u201cpseudo-science\u201d, and sometimes going to the opposite extreme of favoring Practices that one would be hard-pressed to distinguish from what the Technocracy practices).<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly applying the scientific method to mystic principles is a suggested method of explaining the Etherite paradigm in the REvised book, it going over &quot;accupuncture clearly works, so does western medicince so If I make a machine that includes those principles&quot; so I imagine stuff like Demon summoning machines, and... well Chaldea from FGO as very Etherite(though it potentially falls into Hermetic places too)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-24T08:37:37-08:00","id":1276460,"title":"","content":"I'm not familiar with FGO. But yes; the essence of the Etherites is to apply Scientific thinking to a world where magical principles actually work. There's a reason why the Scientific Mystic merit first appeared in the SoE Tradbook. (I hesitate to say \u201cscientific method\u201d, because in many ways the Etherites reject that as unnecessarily reductionist in a universe that isn't reductionist in nature; but they're still very much Scientists, even when the subject matter that they tackle is distinctly supernatural.) However, the Etherites are not a Tradition built primarily around Scientific Mystics: they have their place within the Tradition; but the bulk of the Tradition is made up of Scientists who deal with (usually exotic) technology rather than magic. <br /> <br /> My point is that if you're looking for an approach to combining science and magick that's distinct from what's found in the Society of Ether, you're not going to find it among the Knights if Avalon. Rather, you need to go to a group that embraces the opposite of Scientific Mysticism: the Techgnosi merit from <b>Book of Secrets</b> would be the touchstone for this, producing a faction that applies a Great Mysteries approach to technology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-24T20:02:16-08:00","id":1276552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1275597-successor-to-the-hollow-ones?p=1276460#post1276460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not familiar with FGO. But yes; the essence of the Etherites is to apply Scientific thinking to a world where magical principles actually work. There's a reason why the Scientific Mystic merit first appeared in the SoE Tradbook. (I hesitate to say \u201cscientific method\u201d, because in many ways the Etherites reject that as unnecessarily reductionist in a universe that isn't reductionist in nature; but they're still very much Scientists, even when the subject matter that they tackle is distinctly supernatural.) However, the Etherites are not a Tradition built primarily around Scientific Mystics: they have their place within the Tradition; but the bulk of the Tradition is made up of Scientists who deal with (usually exotic) technology rather than magic.<br /> <br /> My point is that if you're looking for an approach to combining science and magick that's distinct from what's found in the Society of Ether, you're not going to find it among the Knights if Avalon. Rather, you need to go to a group that embraces the opposite of Scientific Mysticism: the Techgnosi merit from <b>Book of Secrets</b> would be the touchstone for this, producing a faction that applies a Great Mysteries approach to technology.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well in Fate Grand Order they have elaborate machines and technologies to exploit mystic principles but whether its Scientifically Mystic or Technognostic would be difficult to determine.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think thought there's also room for &quot;I Have Magick and I have science&quot; as two separate methods of interacting with the world and finding truth within one Paradigm..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-25T16:11:50-08:00","id":1276701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1275597-successor-to-the-hollow-ones?p=1276200#post1276200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kind of like the Society of Ether\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant like not crazy science, more like a Jamesbond Tradition, between Etherite, VA and NWO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-25T16:14:57-08:00","id":1276702,"title":"","content":"Or maybe a psychic tradition mixing Progenitor physiological understanding, Akashics disciplines, and NWO Hyperpsychology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-25T21:03:11-08:00","id":1276738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1275597-successor-to-the-hollow-ones?p=1276701#post1276701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I meant like not crazy science, more like a Jamesbond Tradition, between Etherite, VA and NWO.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The SOE HAS a faction that does that.. its called the Shadow Ministry. Honestly its almost practically a Technocracy in Exile by itself..<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-26T09:26:29-08:00","id":1276814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1275597-successor-to-the-hollow-ones?p=1276702#post1276702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or maybe a psychic tradition mixing Progenitor physiological understanding, Akashics disciplines, and NWO Hyperpsychology.</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds very close / parallel to one of the directions that I would like the Syndicate to be developed according to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}